H5650":"servant/slave","H5002":"utterance"},"ccc":{"0":[1611],"8":[220],"10":[220]},"cccp":{"220":"__P16#","1611":"__P51#"},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Barren Jews in captivity, or Church of the Gentiles, to which alone many of the expressions can be applied. (Calmet) — The Gentiles were before unfruitful, as the Jews will be till towards the latter times. (Worthington)"],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Stakes, to receive so great a family. All the Israelites did not return, and it does not appear that many embraced their religion, as they have done that of Christ."],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Left. To the north and south. Jerusalem increased. But what was it compared with the Christian establishment!"],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Widowhood. Thy former excesses shall be forgotten. (Calmet)"],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","Thee. Hebrew, “Bohalaic (Haydock) shall be your Baalim,” or husband, who was styled Lord, 1 Peter iii. 6. Perhaps he may allude to the two wives, the synagogue and the Church, or to the idols, which should be adored no more."],["haydock",6,null,"haydock","Youth. This enhances her fault. God is pleased to overlook it, in the captives (chap. l. 1.) and Gentiles."],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","Earth. Giving him the rainbow for a sign. My covenant with the Church is equally irrevocable: she is founded on a rock, Matthew xvi. 18. (Calmet) — Christ will no more abandon her than he will drown the world. Some mountains shall be moved out of their place, but she shall not. (Worthington)"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Sapphires. Hebrew, “antimony,” a mineral shining like silver, 4 Kings ix. 30."],["haydock",12,null,"haydock","Bulwarks. Hebrew, windows of crystal; (Ezechiel xxvii. 1[].; Calmet) Protestants, “of agate.” (Haydock) — All this is allegorical, like the redemption of the new Jerusalem, Apocalypse. xxi."],["haydock",13,null,"haydock","Lord, Christ, Jeremias xxxi. 33., and John vi. 45."],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","Thee. The Cutheans rendered the Jews suspected, 1 Esdras iv. 2., and vi. 1"],["haydock",15,null,"haydock","To thee, in the inheritance. This was verified in the Church. We have no accout of many being converted before."],["haydock",16,null,"haydock","Destroy. I can give peace or war. (Calmet) — Septuagint, “but I have created thee not for utter destruction.” (Haydock)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]},"fa":[[1,null,0,"The First Apology","The First Apology, Chapter LIII",0,165,"For all the Gentiles were \"desolate\" of the true God, serving the works of their hands; but the Jews and Samaritans, having the word of God delivered to them by the prophets, and always expecting the Christ, did not recognise Him when He came, except some few, of whom the Spirit of prophecy by Isaiah had predicted that they should be saved."],[1,3,1,"The Proof of the Gospel","Book 3",1,339,"… \"Rejoice, thou barren that bearest not; break forth and cry, thou that travailest not; for more are the children of the desolate, than of her that hath a husband, for the Lord has said, Enlarge the place of thy tent, and the skins of thy hangings peg down, do not spare. Widen thy cords, and strengthen thy pins: spread out still more to the right and left, and thy seed shall inherit the heathen.\" This is the good news the Word gives the Church gathered from the Gentiles scattered throughout the world and stretching from sunrise to sunset, shewn forth very clearly when it says: \"And thy seed shall inherit the Gentiles.\""]],"fau":[["justin-martyr","Justin Martyr",0,"father",null,0],["eusebius","Eusebius of Caesarea",0,"ecclesiastical-writer",null,1,339]],"ftr":[["Ante-Nicene Fathers, vol. 1 (1885)","https://ccel.org/ccel/schaff/anf01"],["W. J. Ferrar, The Proof of the Gospel (SPCK, 1920)"]]}